# Cloud agents
- Default for repo-bound TravelAgency work: code, tests, analysis text, architecture text, CI/Docker file edits, deep PR review. The lead chat stays thin (full brief in, PR or short report out). The lead does the work that needs the server, secrets, chat history, live owner talk, merge, board labels, or wiki publish. Never both on the same artifact.
- Launch: check no branch, PR, or agent exists for the issue; one issue, one agent; branch `type/NN-short-english-slug` via `gh issue develop <NN> --name type/NN-short-english-slug --base main` when the branch does not exist yet (`linkedBranches` only, no closedBy); the agent reads this repo's `.cursor/` rules. Prompt in English with the brief below. Keep it short (about 10-20 lines) and include every item.
- No usage-mode matrix and no scheduled limits refresh (unified Cursor subscription, Oct 28, 2026). Prefer cloud whenever a brief covers the task and the result should not live in lead memory.
- Model: default Grok, medium effort (low mechanical, high multi-file/auth/security, xhigh hard). Opus only if Grok xhigh failed or the task is big and critical; state why.
- Cloud agent limits: regular PR into `main`, never push to `main`, never merge, never edit the wiki or the board, never change a `статус:*` label, no secrets or server access. In the PR «Задача» section link `#NN` only; never write `closes`/`fix`/`fixes`; do not call `addCloseIssueReferences`. Name the `Doc-` page or «вики не затронута». Link the issue to the branch with `gh issue develop` when creating the branch (`project-github-formats.mdc`). Mark the PR ready when CI is green. Final report (English): PR URL, head sha, what changed, tests added, open doubts.
- Acceptance of the agent: the lead owns the result. Strip Cursor PR-body markers and the «Open in Cursor» footer (`gh pr edit --body-file`). Fixes go back to the same agent as a reply. Then the merge gate: CI and Cursor Automations have finished, every open finding has a finished reply, and architect escalation is done when `playbook-step-06-review.mdc` triggers it.

## Orchestrator loop (lead; do not skip)
The lead stays the controller after every cloud agent. Cloud agents do not self-merge, self-accept on dev, advance a column, or talk to the owner.

The loop is the lead's gate on every column that uses an agent. It does not replace Types or columns in `playbook-workflow.mdc`. Set the issue label to the column being started. Launch. Review the result against that column's bar. Accept it or steer a rewrite. Only then set the next column. Do this for Бизнес-анализ, Аналитика, Архитектура, Разбиение, Тест-кейсы, and Разработка.

Разработка starts only when the feature page shows Аналитика, Архитектура, and Тест-кейсы, and no «Решения» row for this slice has an empty «Выбрано». The epic page is not that specification. Epic Бизнес-анализ alone never unlocks feature code. A bug-feature uses the same columns. A typo inside an open feature is not a new issue.

Before merge: no open review finding, green CI, then merge (`playbook-step-06-review.mdc`). After Deploy to dev is green, set Приёмка. Cursor Automations and CI/CD Path A stay; they sit on these columns.

Keep the feature aimed at the epic's problem. If the result drifts, steer a rewrite. Do not adopt a side quest.

1. **Pick and arm:** next Очередь item (`project-github-formats.mdc` «Queue priority»). Finish the current product epic, including its bug-features, before the next roadmap epic. Set the label to the column being started (not a generic in-progress label). Record `Waiting on` / `Next` in `pipeline.md` when the task waits on CI, Deploy, or a cloud agent.
2. **Brief and launch:** one issue, one agent, full brief (`## Brief` below). Name the column. For analysis, architecture, split, or test cases: the agent returns ready Russian text that meets the procedure file for that column. The lead reviews, then publishes. For Разработка: the agent opens the PR.
3. **On result (review, do not redo):** strip Cursor PR markers and the footer; check the diff against the column's bar and the issue scope; formats and secrets (`playbook-git-pr.mdc`, `00-core.mdc`); read open doubts. Do not re-implement the same work in chat.
4. **Steer or advance:** a gap → `reply` to the same agent and wait for the new result. Do not advance `статус:*` until the lead accepts the stage. A wrong or obsolete run → cancel or archive; do not leave an orphan PR or agent without an owner and a next step.
5. **Coordinate:** parallel streams only per `project-travelagency.mdc` «Parallel work». `pipeline.md` is the in-flight map. One owner per task.
6. **Merge:** `playbook-step-06-review.mdc`, then merge order. Notify the owner after merge. The issue stays Разработка until Deploy is green.
7. **Приёмка and docs:** `playbook-step-07-acceptance.mdc`, then Doc- text after merge when the PR named a page (`playbook-step-08-docs.mdc`). Then `статус: готово` and close. Doc- automation gaps stay with the lead.

## Brief (required)
The launch prompt includes all of the following. Do not paste this file or unrelated project guides.

- Goal and acceptance: what must be true when the work stops. Name the type and the column (`playbook-workflow.mdc`). Analysis is product WHY and WHAT only (`playbook-step-01-analysis.mdc`). Feature code waits for Аналитика, Архитектура, and Тест-кейсы on the Feature page, and for a filled «Выбрано» on every decision row for this slice. Epic business analysis alone does not start that code. The agent does not change `статус:*`.
- Links: issue `#NN`, wiki Epic and/or Feature page (section anchor), related `Doc-` pages for current behavior this task touches, and any comment that already decided the approach.
- Architecture context: for feature or code work, name the parent epic's architecture choices and the applicable project-wide constraints (services, contracts, auth).
- Minimal environment context: only the stack touchpoints this task hits. Those touchpoints do not replace the Epic, Feature, and `Doc-` links.
- Hard boundaries: no wiki edits, no board or `статус:*` changes, no merge; no secrets and no server access; stay inside the issue scope and inside the epic's problem; open a regular PR into `main`.
- Where results go: PR sections from `project-github-formats.mdc` («Что сделано», «Зачем», «Как это работает», «Как проверить», «Документация» with the `Doc-` page name or «вики не затронута», «Задача» with `#NN` only). No «Учебный кейс». No `closes` / `fix` / `fixes`. An issue comment, if one is needed, uses «Итог / Подробно / Дальше» (`.cursor/templates/issue-comment.md`). Public text follows `00-core.mdc`.
- Token thrift: minimal diff, no drive-by refactor, stop when the acceptance criteria hold.
